089f5e897077b8edeb318b08e1915fcf8daba86165589d20069a3","file":"preprints/The-complete-Crouzeix-theorem-September-23-2026/build/main.tex","line":132,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"7c43e5460b4c5ce308d615e847aa607d3763efd022912c89d16e3379cc44dbe0","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-complete-Crouzeix-theorem-September-23-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:4f83109ec8a089f5e897077b8edeb318b08e1915fcf8daba86165589d20069a3","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-complete-Crouzeix-theorem-September-23-2026/build/main.tex#L132"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:representation}\nWith the same $\\Omega,A,f,G$ and any chosen minimizing metric in\nTheorem~\\ref{thm:structural}, there is one continuous function\n$\\Lambda:\\T\\to M_n(\\C)$ satisfying\n\\[\n \\Lambda(t)\\succeq0,\\qquad \\int_\\T\\Lambda(t)\\,d\\sigma(t)=I_n,\n\\]\nsuch that, for every positive integer $m$ and every $M_m(\\C)$-valued\nfunction $v$ holomorphic on a neighborhood of $\\overline\\Omega$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:representation-target}\n v[A']=\\int_\\T\\Lambda(t)\\otimes v(G(t))\\,d\\sigma(t),\n \\qquad\n \\|v[A]\\|\\le\\kappa\\max_{\\overline\\Omega}\\|v\\|.\n\\end{equation}\nThe same $S$, $\\Lambda$, and $\\kappa$ work for all $m$ and $v$."}
